etching? It changes relationship? It's still treating compliance as logging practice, just earlier. Introduces new elements (template) but still treats compliance as logging practice. That is slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Score 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane, boring\n\nPre-investment risk classification gate is fairly common in regulated industries. Might be common mundane. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Or 2 = interesting? I think it's a standard best practice, not rare. Could be 2? The reference class is set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give. Many would suggest early compliance scoping. Might be common. I'd say 1.\n\nBut could be 2 = interesting. Hmm.\n\nLet's choose originality 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nProvide output with id and subscale_evidence and subscale.\n\nNeed format? Probably JSON? The prompt says Return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\". Could be lines.\n\nI'll produce structured output:\n\nid: P2293\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\netc.\n\nMake one sentence evidence each.\n\nEnsure one sentence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nacceptability_evidence: The proposal uses a standard compliance review gate and funding control that aligns with legal requirements and business norms. -> score 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Adding a one-page template and a two-week reviewer sign-off requires modest process changes within existing grant workflows. -> score 3\n\napplicability_evidence: The gate directly addresses the lab's need to anticipate Article 12 logging duties before committing R&D resources. -> score 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Early classification improves resource planning for logging but does not itself build the required logs o