lacking Article 12(2)(a)-(c) logs, it ensures traceability records exist when needed for audits and post-market monitoring.\neffectiveness: 4\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly targets how the lab meets Article 12 record-keeping and logging mandates for high-risk prototypes.\napplicability: 4\n\noriginality_evidence: Shift-left compliance gates are unusual in AI labs but not ingenious, representing an interesting process adaptation rather than a surprising invention.\noriginality: 2? Or 3. Hmm. Could be 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. I think 3 is safer. Let's choose 3.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It weaves logging validation into the prototyping pipeline, changing how R&D and compliance interact rather than treating logging as a separate post-hoc task.\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n\nProvide final.\n\n",
