radical changes\". Middleware with Python/C++ SDKs and CI/CD gate is not trivial but maybe reasonably feasible. Might be some changes. I'll give 3.\n\nparadigm_relatedness evidence... score 2\noriginality evidence... score 1\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each before number.\n\nReturn JSON? Probably output with id and fields.\n\nFormat: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably output like:\nP1382\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 4\n...\n\nMake sure order listed: effectiveness, applicability, acceptability, implementability, paradigm_relatedness, originality\n\nProvide one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The middleware automatically captures Article 12(2) events and Annex III 1(a) minimum fields into a tamper-evident store for the system lifetime, directly fulfilling the logging mandate. -> effectiveness:4\n\napplicability_evidence: It targets the stated decision of how to meet Article 12 record-keeping and adapt R&D to avoid market blockage in the EU. -> applicability:4\n\nacceptability_evidence: Centralized tamper-evident logging with CI/CD gating is a standard, non-offensive compliance practice that violates no legal or business norms. -> acceptability:4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Shipping SDKs and a contract test gate requires platform engineering work and process changes across teams, which is reasonably feasible but not trivially cheap. -> implementability:3\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The proposal introduces new logging tools and processes but keeps compliance as a separate logging practice rather than changing the lab's R&D-compliance relationship. -> paradigm_relatedness:2\n\noriginality_evidence: A shared middleware logging layer for regulatory record-keeping is a common, mundane compliance engineering response expected from labs facing EU AI Act obligations. -> originality:1\n\nReturn.\n\n",
