 without regard for workability. Does triage guarantee compliance? It guarantees strictest category fully compliant, others get general recording. Might solve main problem of how to meet logging mandate with scarce resources. I'd say 3.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves identified problem directly related: do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Yes directly related to meeting logging mandate and adapt R&D. So 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nOne-week compliance audit, budget reallocation at next quarterly review. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures. That's 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost? Maybe 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. Budget triage for compliance is acceptable. 4.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each then score.\n\nProvide output.\n\nProbably format:\nid P1928\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality:1\netc.\n\nReturn rating echoing id.\n\nLet's produce concise sentences.\n\nEnsure subscale order listed: originality, paradigm_relatedness, effectiveness, applicability, implementability, acceptability\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\n",
