e compliance content. I'd say 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to this problem. Options: 4 paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 paradigm stretching changes that relationship (logging woven into science, new partners...). 2 slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 paradigm preserving standard compliance and logging practice; lab way unchanged.\n\nThis proposal is carve-out FTE for logging architecture. It's standard compliance practice. It doesn't change relationship, just resource management. So paradigm preserving? Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new element (ring-fence). But still treats compliance as logging practice. Probably 1 or 2. The description: \"introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\" = 2. Carve-out is process change. I'd say 2? Or 1 paradigm preserving standard compliance and logging practice; lab way unchanged. Hmm carve-out mirrors safety-review hours, so it's standard.\n\nProbably paradigm_relatedness = 1 (paradigm preserving). Let's choose 1.\n\nOriginality: degree not only rare but ingenious... 4 not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 interesting. 1 common mundane boring.\n\nDedicated FTE carve-out for compliance is common, mundane. So 1.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably JSON? The instruction says return rating... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Probably list.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1065\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence each.\n\nProvide concise sentences.\n\nImplementability evidence: Allocating eight percent of senior engineering head