g practice.\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Publishing an open-source compliance validator is a common, norm-conforming transparency practice that does not violate legal or social sensibilities.\nacceptability: 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building a schema-based validator as CI checks and documenting it for release requires some engineering changes but is reasonably feasible with existing tooling.\nimplementability: 3\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The validator helps ensure logs meet Article 12(3) minimum fields, contributing to compliance but not itself producing the required logs or covering all logging duties under Article 12(1)-(2).\neffectiveness: 3\n\napplicability_evidence: Validating Annex III log fields directly addresses the lab’s mandate to meet Article 12 record-keeping requirements.\napplicability: 4\n\nReturn.\n\n",
